# Node.js / Backend Rules

## REST shape
- Nouns, not verbs: `GET /api/widgets`, `POST /api/widgets`, `PATCH /api/widgets/:id`.
- Query params for filter/sort/pagination; cursor pagination past ~10k rows.

## Layering (never skip)
`route → controller → service → repository → db`
- Controller: validate input (zod), call service, map result. No DB access.
- Service: business logic. No HTTP.
- Repository: only layer that talks to DB.

## Errors
- One typed error hierarchy; central middleware maps to HTTP.
- Log with request id. Never log secrets or PII.

## Async & performance
- Always `await`. Cache read-heavy endpoints. Long jobs → queue, never block requests.
- Connection pool: `cpu_cores × 2` starting point.
